          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An irrational number is of course a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number"} number
            that is not
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
            number; in this case, it is interesting to consider such numbers for two reasons:
          %ul
            %li Historically, it was an important discovery that irrational real numbers exist.
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              of all irrational real numbers is interesting in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+analysis"} constructive analysis
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computability"} computability
              theory, and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descriptive+set+theory"} descriptive set theory
          %p Of course, there are also various theorems about general classes of numbers that distinguish rational from irrational numbers.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_the_real_numbers In the real numbers
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+function"} affine function
            on the real numbers consists of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and real number
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            such that for all real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = a x + b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
            at zero
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi x
                  %mn .0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda x.0
            is an affine function where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = 0
            %strong irrational
            if for all affine functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            coefficients, if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi λ
                    %mi x
                    %mn .0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \lambda x.0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \neq a
          %p
            Alternatively, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is
            %strong irrational
            if given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            (thought of as a real number), the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|x - a|}
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
          %p
            These two definitions are equivalent in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %strong weakly irrational
            while the latter definition is called
            %strong strongly irrational
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong strictly irrational
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of irrational real numbers (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of the set of real numbers) is variously denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔹
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{B}
            (in various fonts). The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            stand for ‘irrational’, while the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔹
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{B}
            stands for ‘Baire’ (see the next paragraph). Here we will use
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
          %p
            We may give
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+structure"} topology
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            is sometimes called
            = succeed ";" do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baire+space+of+irrational+numbers"} Baire space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+structure"} uniform structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baire+space"} Baire space
            as a space to which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baire+category+theorem"} Baire category theorem
            applies; however,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            is an example of such a space.)
          %h3#as_nonrepeating_radix_expansions As non-repeating radix expansions
          %p
            There is another definition of irrational number, common in the prealgebra and high school algebra literature, which directly defines the irrational numbers in terms of base 10 infinite radix expansions. (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radix+notation"} radix notation
          %p
            Let the natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \gt 1
            denote the base of the radix expansion,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, b)
            denote the half-open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            of all natural numbers less than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansions are elements of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times [0, b)^\mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, d)
            consists of an integer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and a sequence of digits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(n)
            in the base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansion. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/series"} series
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{n = 0}^\infty i + \frac{d(n)}{b^{n + 1}}
          %p
            can be shown to be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+sequence"} Cauchy sequence
          %p
            The set of repeating base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansion is the subset of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times [0, b)^\mathbb{N}
            such that for pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, d)
            in the subset, there exist natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and positive natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            such that the sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi m
                  %mo .
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda m.d(m + k)
            factors through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi m
                  %mo .
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi n
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda m.d(m + k):\mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z} \to [0, b)
          %p
            Two base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, d)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j, e)
            are said to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apart from
            each other if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \neq j
            or there exists a natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(n) \neq e(n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo #
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo .
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i, d) \# (j, e) \coloneqq (i \neq j) \vee \exists n \in \mathbb{N}.d(n) \neq e(n)
          %p
            A base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is
            %em strictly non-repeating
            if it is apart from every repeating base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansion. An
            %strong irrational number
            is a strictly non-repeating base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansion.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{n = 0}^\infty i + \frac{d(n)}{b^{n + 1}}
          %p
            given by a non-repeating base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansion. However, it is still the case that strictly irrational numbers which are also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
            are interdefinable with strictly non-repeating base
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            infinite radix expansions.
          %h3#in_archimedean_integral_domains In Archimedean integral domains
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+integral+domain"} Archimedean integral domain
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \subseteq R
            being a integral subdomain of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
            is irrational if for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{Z}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert a \vert \gt 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi r
                    %mo −
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert a \cdot r - b \vert \gt 0
          %p
            The set of
            %strong irrational numbers
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is defined as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕁
                    %mi R
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi r
                  %mo −
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}_R \coloneqq \{r \in R \vert \forall a, b \in \mathbb{Z}. (\vert a \vert \gt 0) \wedge (\vert a \cdot r - b \vert \gt 0) \}
          %h3#in_integral_domains_with_a_padic_norm In integral domains with a p-adic norm
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+norm"} p-adic norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert(-)\vert_p
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \subseteq R
            being a integral subdomain of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
            is irrational if for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbb{Z}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi p
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert a \vert_p \gt 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi r
                    %mo −
                    %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi p
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert a \cdot r - b \vert_p \gt 0
          %p
            The set of
            %strong irrational numbers
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is defined as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝕁
                    %mi R
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo .
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi p
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi r
                  %mo −
                  %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi p
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}_R \coloneqq \{r \in R \vert \forall a, b \in \mathbb{Z}. (\vert a \vert_p \gt 0) \wedge (\vert a \cdot r - b \vert_p \gt 0) \}
          %h2#history History
          %p
            The followers of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pythagoras"} Pythagoras
            believed that ‘All is number’, meaning what we now call (positive)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            are
            %span.newWikiWord
              commensurable
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/commensurable+quantities"} ?
            in the sense that there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi m
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = m u
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = n u
            for some natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %em false
            is also attributed to the Pythagoreans (but the legends of punishment for this secret date from several hundred years later). Greek mathematicians developed further the theory of irrational numbers, up to the general theory of magnitudes (which we may now regard as a theory of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+real+numbers"} positive real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eudoxus"} Eudoxus
            in Book X of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclid%27s+Elements"} Euclid's Elements
          %p
            Mathematicians coming from the cultures of the Islamic Golden Age (particularly
            = succeed ")" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Abu Kamil
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Abu+Kamil"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            of
            %span.newWikiWord
              Al-Khwarizmi
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Al-Khwarizmi"} ?
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+roots"} square roots
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/roots"} roots
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omar+Khayyam"} Omar Khayyam
            developed a general method to find the real roots of any cubic
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            = succeed "s)," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                radical number
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/radical+number"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^5 + 2 x + 1
          %p
            Later, European mathematicians of the early modern era (particularly
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Cardano
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Gerolamo+Cardano"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Tartaglia
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Tartaglia"} ?
            = succeed ")" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Ferrari
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Lodovico+Ferrari"} ?
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+number"} imaginary number
            %span.newWikiWord
              Lambert
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Johann+Lambert"} ?
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adrien-Marie+Legendre"} Legendre
            succeeded in proving the irrationality of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pi"} pi
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e"} e
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^5 + 2x + 1
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number"} algebraic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Hermite"} Hermite
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Lindemann
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ferdinand+von+Lindemann"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonhard+Euler"} Euler
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph-Louis+Lagrange"} Lagrange
            popularized
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continued+fraction"} continued fraction
          %p
            During the
            %span.newWikiWord
              arithmetization of analysis
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/arithmetization+of+analysis"} ?
            in the 19th century, people sometimes wrote of the problem of ‘defining irrational numbers’. The actual issue here was defining real numbers in general; one could define rational numbers algebraically, leaving only the irrational numbers as the problem. However, this may be a red herring; one could just as easily define
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number"} algebraic number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{e}
            are irrational that work on this problem came to life. On the other hand, it's not clear that anybody could completely work out the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order"} order
            properties of algebraic numbers without already coming upon
            = succeed "'s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Dedekind"} Dedekind
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{2}
            posed no difficulty to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitist+mathematics"} finitist
            methods used by such algebraists as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leopold+Kronecker"} Leopold Kronecker
          %p
            To this day, there are various specific real numbers (such as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo +
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi + \mathrm{e}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+number"} Euler–Mascheroni constant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation
            of this statement can be proved for any real number). The question of whether
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %msqrt
                      %mn 2
                    %msqrt
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\sqrt{2}}^{\sqrt{2}}
            is rational or irrational is part of a famous illustration of the nature of constructive vs nonconstructive proof. (Namely, there is a cheap and easy nonconstructive proof that there exist irrational numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^b
            is rational: let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{2}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            be either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{2}
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %msqrt
                        %mn 2
                      %msqrt
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\sqrt{2}}^{\sqrt{2}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %msqrt
                      %mn 2
                    %msqrt
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\sqrt{2}}^{\sqrt{2}}
            turns out to be irrational, by a constructive version of the
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Gelfond–Schneider theorem
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Gelfond-Schneider+theorem"} ?
            = succeed ")" do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The Baire space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}^{\mathbb{N}}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
            copies of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continued+fraction"} continued fraction
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+space"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polish+space"} Polish space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            is itself a Polish space.
          %p
            As a subset of the real line,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+set"} full set
            (meaning that its complement, the set of rational numbers, is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+set"} null
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cantor+space"} Cantor space
            may be identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            (but this does not agree with the usual inclusions into
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fan+theorem"} fan theorem
            states precisely that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            (when thought of as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober
            or that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
            (when thought of as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locale"} topological/spatial/has enough points
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            and in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+mathematics"} intuitionistic mathematics
            but fails in other forms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %h2#continued_fractions Continued fractions
          %p
            (Main article:
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continued+fraction"} continued fraction
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ;
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a_0;a_1,a_2,a_3,\ldots]
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequence"} infinite sequence
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi a
                                %mn 3
                              %mo +
                              %mi ⋯
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0 + \frac{1}{a_1 + \frac{1}{a_2 + \frac{1}{a_3 + \cdots}}} .
          %p
            By truncating this expression after
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorems Theorems
            %p
              This is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+sequence"} Cauchy sequence
              whose limit is irrational. Furthermore, every irrational number has a unique representation in this way. Yet more, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              thus shown between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{J}
              and the infinitary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{N}^+ \times \mathbb{N}^+ \times \mathbb{N}^+ \times \cdots
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              when the two sets are given their usual
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+structure"} topologies
          %p
            The usual proofs of these theorems are entirely
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}^{\mathbb{N}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            or as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}^{\mathbb{N}}
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pi"} pi
            %li
              %p
